      "writtenOn": "2022-01-25T07:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Unclear how one would prioritize both.\n\nThat\u0027s the point. Some apps prefer a network with lower latency but lower bandwidth. Some apps prefer a network with higher latency but higher bandwidth.\n\nA network with both is just a faster network. If it\u0027s the same cost, then why should we not make it the default network of the device always ? If it\u0027s more expensive, then we need access control. But there is none. So in T, it doesn\u0027t really make sense as a use case. The capability names reflect that.",
      "parentUuid": "2a290232_d95b5d8a",
      "revId": "7baea05a14693583b55a26dc33be4cde56f2ba41",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
